(Bug #32 - a flag read inside a function body was typed boolean whatever
 it was declared as. The analyzer kept flag names in a bare set and
 answered Type::Boolean for any of them, so `Set target to voxpath.`
 inside a function failed with "cannot assign boolean to 'target', which
 is a text". Top level escaped it because the declaration's own type was
 still in scope; only the in-function path consulted the hardcode.

 All three flag types must survive a round trip through a function.)
a flag called voxpath is "-V" or "--vox", it is a text with default "path".
a flag called optseed is "-s" or "--seed", it is a number with default 7.
a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
Parse flags.

a text called got_text is "unset".
a number called got_number is 0.
a boolean called got_boolean is true.

To apply.
    Set got_text to voxpath.
    Set got_number to optseed.
    Set got_boolean to verbose.

apply.
Print "text:{got_text}".
Print "number:{got_number}".
Print "boolean:{got_boolean}".
